  "description": "WEMNUB crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n n c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H146 O42 S8 Tb9 9+,2(C1 H4 O1),9(Cl1 1-),2.6(C3 H7 N1 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 10 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2C (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2D (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2E (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2F (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2G (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.608-5.103 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.73-173.47°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {[Tb9(μ5-OH)2(μ3-OH)8(OCH3)9(TC4A)2(H2O)24]Cl9}·2.6DMF. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ5-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 24 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
